1) Based on some condition if you want to do any job then we can go for if conditional construction
2) If is a keyword which requires a conditions(mandatory)
3) If the condition is true if body will be executed once.
4) If the conditions is false if body will skipped.
5) If programmer is not giving any body {} explicitly, then the compiler will take the body as starts from keyword until the first (;) semicolon. This rule is applicable for if,else,while,for,do.
6) If we have only one statement in the body then pair {} are also optional.
7) In C language ,in the place of condition we can write whatever we want , compiler will check either it is 0 or non zero , if it is nonzero treated as true ,
if it is 0 treated as false

Syntax:

if(condition)------|
{                  |
                   |(true)
if body; <---------|

}

